Rule 2 (unknown dimensions require partial evaluation)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : bool} |= if (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = -1) then v_2 = true
>>
Rule 3 (scalar tensors are trivially constant in value range)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 0 then min(v_1) = max(v_1)
>>
Rule 4 (non-empty tensors have well-defined min/max ordering)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0 then min(v_1) ≤ max(v_1)
>>
Rule 5 (shape index variable is always within valid bounds)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : 0 ≤ i ∧ i < ndim(v_1)
>>
Rule 6 (partial flag is a boolean selector)
{v_2 : bool} |= v_2 = true ∨ v_2 = false
>>
Rule 8 (non-partial evaluation requires statically known shape)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: bool} |= v_2 = true ∨ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 10 (scalars are always acceptable; non-scalars follow partial/shape rule)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: bool} |= if ndim(v_1) = 0 then true else v_2 = true ∨ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 11 (bool or string tensors impose no extra restriction beyond type; others follow partial/shape rule)
